sample M3-c156 L09 grade T | For a real symmetric A, what is the squared Frobenius distance that eigenvalue clipping at floor epsilon moves A? => Assuming F1 to F4 of Lesson 4, ||A - A_epsilon||_F^2 equals the sum over the eigenvalues lambda_i below epsilon of (epsilon - lambda_i)^2 (Proposition 3.3(a)).
